Serialize tcp_socket writes in kcenon/network_system 093691d9

pacs_system carries this patch until its network_system pin contains an
equivalent fix. See docs/SOUP.md, "network_system overlapping writes (#1319)".

tcp_socket::async_send started asio::async_write for every call, but Asio
allows one write at a time on a stream. When a write completed only in part,
because the peer read slowly, the next one ran inside it and interleaved the
bytes, which broke DICOM PDU framing. Sends now wait in a queue and start one
at a time on the socket's executor. Both copies of tcp_socket.h change, since
translation units include either one and must agree on the class layout.

The checkout action applies it to the index after cloning the pin and fails
when it no longer applies. Remove this file once the pin moves past a
network_system revision that serializes these writes.

